       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This dose is twice that limit and raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't change that.\n\nIt may be a typo. These are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
