     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the safety problem, and I can't verify any rationale behind it. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. The main risk is metformin-associated lactic acidosis.\n\nThese options would let the order go through:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit.** Tell me which one and I'll enter it right away, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Get pharmacy or attending review.** If there's a specific reason for the higher dose, the pharmacist or the attending of record can review it and enter or override it through the hospital's usual process. That process includes dose-range checks that I can't replace.\n\nI can also enter the order with a note for pharmacy asking them to verify the dose, but only at a dose within the standard range."
      }
     ],
